{"ticker":"BALAMINES","symbol":"BALAMINES","instrumentId":3099186,"name":"Balaji Amines","industry":"NSE-Chemicals-Specialty","about":"Balaji Amines Ltd. (BAL), is a prominent Indian manufacturer of Aliphatic Amines, Specialty Chemicals, and Pharma Excipients. Initially set up to meet the growing demand for value-based chemicals, BAL began producing Methyl Amines in 1989, later expanding to Ethyl Amines and their derivatives. With a state-of-the-art manufacturing facility in Tamalwadi Village, Solapur, Maharashtra, BAL uses advanced digital control systems and robust R&D facilities to ensure high-quality, cost-effective products. Recognized internationally for its stringent quality standards, BAL is ISO 9001:2015 certified and continues to supply major global markets with its diverse product range.","website":"www.balajiamines.com","location":"Solapur, INDIA","exchange":"NSE","fetchedAt":"2026-11-20T13:07:05.407Z","basis":"consolidated","price":{"value":1878.3,"changePct":-1.0483616057317506,"week52High":2566.8,"week52Low":977.2},"stats":[{"label":"Market capitalization","value":"₹6,086 Cr"},{"label":"Sales","value":"₹1,650 Cr"},{"label":"Shares in float","value":"14,580,000"},{"label":"No. of funds","value":"80"},{"label":"Shares held by funds","value":"1,536,713"},{"label":"Dividend yield","value":"0.59%"},{"label":"Book value","value":"3.08"},{"label":"U/D vol ratio","value":"0.9"},{"label":"LTDebt / equity","value":"3.0%"},{"label":"Alpha","value":"0.25"},{"label":"Beta","value":"1.52"},{"label":"EPS growth rate","value":"-17%"},{"label":"P/E ratio","value":"25.6"},{"label":"5-year P/E range","value":"23–47"},{"label":"Return on equity","value":"8.5%"},{"label":"Cash flow (INR)","value":"56.8"},{"label":"Volume","value":"71,808"},{"label":"Avg volume (50d)","value":"224,241"},{"label":"Master score","value":"70"},{"label":"EPS rating","value":"69"},{"label":"Price strength","value":"82"},{"label":"Group rank","value":"66"},{"label":"Acc/Dis rating","value":"B"}]